1
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:24,660
(Chen Hewen returns to Signal House)

2
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:27,560
He got off work early.

3
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,280
Hello.

4
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,040
Hello.

5
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:31,980
(Smiles)
Liang Xiaoyu.

6
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:32,960
Are you the first one here?

7
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:34,400
Is anyone else here?

8
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,040
Looks like Si is back too.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,320
Why are you home so early?

10
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:38,840
Well,

11
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,400
I finished work a little early today.

12
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:44,960
Are you going to play the piano?

13
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,040
I was going to practice
before you guys got here.

14
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,160
Can I listen?

15
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:49,960
I'm not very good.

16
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:52,000
I haven't practiced enough.

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,720
Can you play?

18
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:53,680
Of course not.

19
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:54,840
Okay.

20
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:55,720
I'll get you a bottle of water.

21
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:57,160
Thanks.

22
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:00,680
We'll cut up that durian later.

23
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:01,440
Sure, no problem.

24
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:03,400
Okay. Let's cut it outside.

25
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:03,920
Okay.

26
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:05,760
We definitely have to eat this outside.

27
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,160
The smell is so strong.

28
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:09,480
Let's go.

29
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,240
Let's go. I'll carry it.

30
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:13,760
You look great in that.

31
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:15,320
You looked pretty good yesterday too.

32
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:16,440
Actually, it's still

33
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:17,760
a little chilly outside.

34
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:18,840
Yeah.

35
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:20,680
And it's pretty open up ahead.

36
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:24,600
I can already smell it.

37
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:25,400
Honestly,

38
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,440
I need to figure this out.

39
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:28,280
Let's take a look.

40
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:30,740
(Durian escapes)

41
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:31,320
This...

42
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:34,080
It should be ripe already.

43
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:35,040
It'll split open on its own.

44
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:35,480
Look.

45
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:36,280
Be careful. It'll prick you.

46
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:36,760
Careful, it'll prick you.

47
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:37,400
It's okay. I'll go slowly.

48
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:37,840
I'll go really slowly.

49
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,160
It's sharp.

50
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,760
This piece.

51
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,600
I'll handle this one.

52
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:43,480
You do that one.

53
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:45,440
It's okay.
I'm just worried you'll get pricked.

54
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:49,920
Still, be careful with your hand.

55
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:55,920
From this side.

56
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:57,440
Have this piece.

57
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:58,280
I think this size is just right.

58
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:01,560
I want this one.

59
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:03,520
Honestly,

60
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:04,560
this is way too small.

61
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:06,440
About the durian yesterday,

62
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,440
I was actually...

63
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:08,080
When we were in the car

64
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:08,680
talking back then,

65
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,000
didn't I say

66
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,320
that if I got the chance,
I'd buy a durian,

67
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:11,520
and we'd

68
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,200
take it outside

69
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,280
and try it?

70
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,360
I honestly didn't expect

71
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:16,880
so many people

72
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:17,840
would be okay with the smell.

73
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:18,840
Yeah, I didn't expect it either.

74
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:19,640
Everyone really loved it.

75
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,800
That really surprised me.

76
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:30,000
You're not that busy today.

77
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,600
I might've just been
a little busy these past few days,

78
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:33,480
and I felt

79
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,920
a little tired.

80
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,680
Happy tired.

81
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,720
(Liang Xiaoyu)
It's a good thing.

82
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:41,960
Yeah.

83
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,400
It actually makes me happy.

84
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:44,600
If I can put more time

85
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,400
into the things I enjoy,

86
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:46,960
like

87
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:48,120
bringing my work into them,

88
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,080
I think

89
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,520
I'd have even more motivation.

90
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:51,840
Exactly.

91
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,400
That's how I see it.

92
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,160
Yeah.

93
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:54,920
No matter whether

94
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:55,880
it works out in the end,

95
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:56,680
I really enjoy

96
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,560
the process.

97
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,120
I don't really like
having nothing to do.

98
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,720
Does having nothing to do
make you anxious?

99
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,560
Not really.

100
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,800
When I have free time,

101
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,920
I might work out or travel.

102
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,840
My grandma loves traveling,

103
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:13,600
so she took me

104
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:14,560
to a lot of places when I was little.

105
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,400
The places from my childhood
mean a lot to me

106
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,920
because those were the places

107
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:22,840
where my grandparents raised me.

108
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:23,960
We used to go see the peach blossoms

109
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,080
every summer.

110
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:29,160
That place probably

111
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,560
doesn't even look the same anymore.

112
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:32,720
But still,

113
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:34,120
I like going back there.

114
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:36,800
It means a lot

115
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,720
to me.

116
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:38,840
I have so many

117
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,040
good memories

118
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:42,080
that were made there

119
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:42,720
when I was little.

120
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,920
Chen Hewen seems really relaxed around her.

121
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:48,040
He can finally let his guard down.

122
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,920
He doesn't feel like

123
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:51,480
having to stay tense all the time.
That's exhausting.

124
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:52,160
And Liang Xiaoyu

125
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,200
just keeps listening.

126
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:56,320
If you're talking about sharing,

127
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,960
I feel like with these memories,

128
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:58,880
when I try

129
00:03:58,880 --> 00:03:59,680
to share them,

130
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,280
I don't really know

131
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,480
how to put them into words.

132
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,200
I'm afraid I won't be able

133
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,320
to express how I felt back then.

134
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,240
I think what you just said

135
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,800
was really well put.

136
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,000
She's affirming him.

137
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:12,800
Yeah.

138
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,800
Putting your thoughts into words

139
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:17,960
is something really meaningful.

140
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:18,680
Exactly.

141
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,800
Some old stories,

142
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,040
when you tell them again

143
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:24,200
and then share them with someone,

144
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,560
they become new memories.

145
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,840
That's beautifully said.

146
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:33,380
(Old stories shared with new people
become new memories)

147
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,200
I've been talking
about what I went through as a kid.

148
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,120
What about your childhood?

149
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,240
Do you want to share some stories too?

150
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:45,760
My childhood was pretty normal.

151
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:47,200
I feel like you were the kind of kid

152
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:49,480
who was very mature and well-behaved,

153
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,760
and did really well in school.

154
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,200
I just studied
whatever I was interested in.

155
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:57,560
I was more into science.

156
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:58,720
Science.

157
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,840
My favorite book as a kid

158
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,120
was We Love Science.

159
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:01,920
We Love Science?

160
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,200
Have you read it?

161
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,480
Of course I have.

162
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,160
That's great.

163
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,720
I really loved that class as a kid.

164
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,520
What was it called again?

165
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:11,440
Morality and the Rule of Law.

166
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,920
I paid extra attention in that class.

167
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:17,640
I thought you meant

168
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:18,640
the class was so easy,

169
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:20,440
you'd just mess around in class.

170
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:21,920
No.

171
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:22,840
Not that.

172
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,440
I just remembered a saying.

173
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:27,280
It goes something like,

174
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:28,600
a person's character

175
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,080
is shaped during kindergarten.

176
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:31,720
I actually think
that makes a lot of sense.

177
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:36,360
If you put it that way,

178
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,600
what did I watch in elementary school?

179
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,560
I watched...

180
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:42,680
Ultraman.

181
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,080
Yeah.

182
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,240
That's pretty wholesome.

183
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:47,680
You've been "a light of justice"
since you were a kid.

184
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,240
Yeah, of course.

185
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:52,400
I saw everyone as a "monster"

186
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,720
and just wanted to go after them.

187
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,200
"A light of justice".

188
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,240
Believe in the light.

189
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,160
What are your hobbies?

190
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:08,480
Badminton. I really enjoy it too.

191
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,720
I've been playing badminton

192
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,440
for over four years now.

193
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,080
We're actually pretty similar.

194
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:18,960
I have a lot of hobbies too,

195
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:22,800
but I don't keep adding new ones.

196
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,160
I'd rather keep getting better

197
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:26,120
at what I do.

198
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,320
Yeah.

199
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:31,360
I don't lose interest that easily.

200
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,280
People ask me,

201
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,040
"You play badminton every day."

202
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,280
"Why don't you try another sport?"

203
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,400
But I just think,

204
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,960
if I keep learning and improving,

205
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:39,520
maybe I can take it
to the next level, right?

206
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:45,280
I bet you look really good
when you play.

207
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,200
Play badminton with me sometime.

208
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,360
Sure. No problem.

209
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,160
Of course.

210
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,320
Maybe you can teach me piano sometime.

211
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,000
Sure.

212
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,080
I'll teach you right now. Come on.

213
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,760
Is it hard? Just wondering.

214
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:04,560
Not at all.

215
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,400
I actually took a lesson before.

216
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:07,920
I took one class.

217
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:11,680
Someone once said

218
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,840
my fingers look pretty long.

219
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,000
Let me see.

220
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,940
(Coming closer)

221
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,220
(Moves closer)

222
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,640
Your fingers really are long.

223
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:22,560
Both their hands look great.

224
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,440
Look.

225
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:35,600
The stars are beautiful.

226
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,520
Yeah. The stars are all coming out.

227
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:48,360
Liang Xiaoyu

228
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,200
keeps the conversation moving

229
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:50,520
at her own pace.

230
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,120
I feel like their conversation

231
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:54,080
moves a little faster.

232
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,160
Because Liang Xiaoyu is steady.

233
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:56,600
She listens

234
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,280
and encourages him.

235
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,680
She's completely the guiding type,

236
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:00,440
almost like an older sister.

237
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:01,720
Liang Xiaoyu makes her approval

238
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,760
of Chen Hewen

239
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:05,080
very clear and specific.

240
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:05,880
For example, with Ultraman,

241
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:07,320
she said, "You're a 'light of justice.'"

242
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:08,560
She was basically saying,
"I understand why you like this."

243
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,600
"It represents justice."

244
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:10,000
Then he said,

245
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:10,720
"I'm so tired."

246
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:11,880
And she said,
"But what you're busy with"

247
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:12,320
"is something"

248
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:13,760
"that makes you happy."

249
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,720
"That's why you'll be happy."

250
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,320
Her approval was expressed

251
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,640
through specific things,

252
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:20,760
so Chen Hewen could clearly feel

253
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:21,920
that she approved of him.

254
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:24,280
Before he even realized it,

255
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:25,800
Chen Hewen had already
opened up to Liang Xiaoyu

256
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,080
about his childhood stories.

257
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,240
Without realizing it,

258
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:31,080
he may have also developed
a sense of trust in Liang Xiaoyu.

259
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:32,520
That's how their relationship

260
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:33,800
gradually began to take shape.

261
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:35,520
They were able to get deeper

262
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:37,480
into sharing personal information.

263
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,360
Compared to the others,

264
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:40,000
their conversations

265
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,040
felt more mature

266
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:42,160
and natural.

267
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:44,000
Chen Hewen and Sha Yue'er

268
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,000
were constantly testing each other.

269
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,960
Neither of them let their guard down.

270
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,000
In his interactions

271
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,520
with Liang Xiaoyu,

272
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:51,880
there's something called

273
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:52,960
"complementary validation".

274
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,680
From the moment we met,

275
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,000
I'd ask what you liked,

276
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,520
what your hobbies were,

277
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:58,240
and show my approval.

278
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,560
Then I'd say,

279
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:00,800
"That's really nice."

280
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,000
The way you expressed that

281
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
was a really good response.

282
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,400
Then there's validation.

283
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:04,920
Like she said,

284
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,440
"We actually have things in common."

285
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,440
So you can see

286
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,280
that the word "validation"

287
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,360
has led to many different forms

288
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,160
of connection.

289
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:12,320
So I think what they have

290
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,120
is a kind of

291
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,240
complementary validation.

292
