and suck the meat out,

588
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:50,960
right?

589
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,240
That sounds pretty complicated.

590
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:54,080
I've never made anything
that complicated.

591
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:55,040
Is it complicated?

592
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:55,800
It's just ginger and scallions,

593
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:57,120
right?

594
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,720
Complicated? It's easy.

595
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:04,680
Shell-on seafood is the hardest to prep.

596
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:05,920
Actually, it's not too bad.

597
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:06,800
It's manageable.

598
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:07,600
They're getting competitive.

599
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:11,720
Guys,

600
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:12,880
should we add a vegetable?

601
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:13,600
I can make a vegetable dish.

602
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,120
Sure.

603
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,480
What vegetables can you make?

604
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,160
I bought some snow peas.

605
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:18,960
Does everyone eat them?

606
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:20,000
Sure.

607
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:22,480
Do you want garlic?

608
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,800
I can chop up some garlic.

609
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,240
I want garlic.

610
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:26,000
How many cloves?

611
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,200
I want sliced garlic.

612
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:28,360
What are you making?

613
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,360
Kung Pao chicken.

614
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:32,480
Wow, you're good.

615
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:33,680
(Steps forward)

616
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:34,200
Chef.

617
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:35,400
Show us what you've got!

618
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,160
It might not taste good,

619
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,840
but it should be edible.

620
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,320
That applies

621
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,320
to me tomorrow too.

622
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:49,360
It might not taste good,

623
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:50,280
but it'll definitely be cooked.

624
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:51,160
I'll make sure I fry it

625
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:52,600
until it's fully cooked, okay?

626
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:53,920
Do you want
the garlic slices thick or thin?

627
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,720
Thin. Garlic slices and ginger slices.

628
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:57,780
(Glances)

629
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:00,000
For ginger slices,
cut them on a diagonal?

630
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,040
Either way works. Up to you.

631
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:05,200
Did you notice
there's one photo missing?

632
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,080
One photo?

633
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:07,120
I came to get one yesterday.

634
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:07,720
None of you took one?

635
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:08,480
You really took one?

636
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:09,680
I really did.

637
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:12,600
Which one did you take?

638
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:13,720
I took this one too.

639
00:19:15,180 --> 00:19:16,140
(Glances)

640
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:20,000
(Slowly approaching)
We hung up a bunch of photos yesterday.

641
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:20,360
See?

642
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:21,240
Let me show you, Sha Yue'er.

643
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,080
When did you take these?

644
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,000
Yesterday.

645
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,400
(Leaning closer)
Chen Hewen is really going all out.

646
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:31,580
(Takes it)

647
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:33,240
One on each side.

648
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:34,360
They both look great.

649
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:35,400
But honestly,

650
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:36,320
I kind of nailed this one.

651
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:40,240
I took this one.

652
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:41,200
Okay, I took a really good one.

653
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,400
Well, this one looks great.

654
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:44,480
This one looks great.

655
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:50,760
And I told you guys

656
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:51,440
to show your faces.

657
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:52,800
I like it too.

658
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:55,120
Which strand of yarn
do you think you just...

659
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:55,680
All I can say is...

660
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:56,600
Which strand of hair looks like me?

661
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:57,600
Everyone's convinced.

662
00:19:57,600 --> 00:19:58,400
You're definitely him.

663
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,120
I'm really taking these two with me.

664
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,480
Okay, let's get the food.

665
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:11,440
Let me see.

666
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,120
Nobody's talking anymore.

667
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:19,920
Silence.

668
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:23,400
These four.

669
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:24,920
Seriously.

670
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:26,640
Always something happening
in the kitchen.

671
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:28,720
Hello.

672
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:29,560
Hello.

673
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:31,840
Hello.

674
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:32,320
Hi.

675
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:32,720
Hi.

676
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:33,640
Hi, Yu Yang.

677
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:34,880
I need your help.

678
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:36,240
(Come closer)
Those ribs.

679
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,440
The ribs?

680
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:38,000
Okay.

681
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,240
Need any help?

682
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,040
Guys.

683
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:40,800
(Laughs)

684
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:41,640
I guess we do.

685
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,800
I feel like Sha Yue'er gets happy

686
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:44,480
the moment she hears Chen Hewen's voice.

687
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,400
Can you mix some water into the starch?

688
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:47,680
Starch?

689
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:48,240
Do you know where it is?

690
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:48,640
Starch.

691
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:49,480
Look for it.

692
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,440
Yu Yang, do you know
where the starch is?

693
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:53,040
Starch. I saw it yesterday.

694
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:56,520
I think it's over there.

695
00:20:57,800 --> 00:20:59,240
Do you need potato starch

696
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,520
or cornstarch?

697
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:01,200
Either is fine.

698
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:02,260
(Looking)
Potato starch.

699
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,080
How much? A spoonful?

700
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,640
It's just for thickening the sauce.

701
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,480
It depends on how thick

702
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:10,400
you want the sauce.

703
00:21:11,860 --> 00:21:13,260
(Walks closer)

704
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:13,800
(Walks away)
So the starch...

705
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:14,920
Is anyone free?

706
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:15,920
Starch...

707
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:17,080
I'm free.

708
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:18,880
Come peel this.

709
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,680
Liang Xiaoyu's one simple sentence

710
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:22,160
completely changed the whole mood.

711
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,840
Come peel this.

712
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,200
- Look at her taking charge.
- This one.

713
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:26,800
Take a look.

714
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:27,960
You just need to remove

715
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:28,760
the ends.

716
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:29,720
Because they're too tough.

717
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:33,000
I'll put on gloves.

718
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:33,720
Do I need to?

719
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:34,800
I can just wash my hands.

720
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:38,040
Starch, guys...

721
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:39,280
Does anyone know where it is?

722
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,120
I found it.

723
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:44,520
Here.

724
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:46,320
Right here.

725
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:47,200
Okay.

726
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:48,520
Just add some water to it,

727
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:49,640
right, Sha Yue'er?

728
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:50,480
Yeah.

729
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,000
This is just trimming off the ends.

730
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:01,400
Is this enough? Not quite.

731
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:10,800
Is tap water okay?

732
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:11,760
- Or do we need...
- It's fine.

733
00:22:14,360 --> 00:22:15,520
I don't think this has any strings.

734
00:22:15,520 --> 00:22:16,600
If there aren't any,
don't worry about it.

735
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:19,600
I almost threw out the beans

736
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:20,920
and threw the strings into the bowl.

737
00:22:22,600 --> 00:22:23,760
Sha Yue'er isn't happy anymore.

738
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:24,800
She actually cares.

739
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:37,520
Is this enough?

740
00:22:38,120 --> 00:22:39,080
A little more.

741
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:43,720
A little more starch, right?

742
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:44,040
Right.

743
00:22:44,040 --> 00:22:44,800
Oh my gosh.

744
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:45,560
These four.

745
00:23:05,560 --> 00:23:06,320
Can you help me find

746
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:07,280
the MSG?

747
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:08,120
MSG?

748
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:13,120
The MSG is right here.

749
00:23:13,120 --> 00:23:13,640
It's not here?

750
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:14,320
MSG.

751
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:15,320
It's right here.

752
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:18,360
That's chicken bouillon.

753
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:20,280
It's basically MSG
with a few other things added.

754
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:21,280
It's different.

755
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:23,040
Let me see.

756
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:24,120
Chicken bouillon.

757
00:23:24,440 --> 00:23:25,040
MSG.

758
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:26,440
This...

759
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,560
This is chicken bouillon too.

760
00:23:28,780 --> 00:23:30,900
(Checking again and again)

761
00:23:30,920 --> 00:23:32,280
It looks like
we only have chicken bouillon.

762
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:33,680
I saw some a few days ago.

763
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:35,440
Really?

764
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:36,560
Really.

765
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:37,560
Need any help, Yu Yang?

766
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,440
No, I'm good.

767
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:40,200
No, you need to give me

768
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:41,600
something to do.

769
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:43,480
Make you do something...

770
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:44,080
Make you do something.

771
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:45,560
Make you.

772
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:46,360
Make you do something.

773
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:49,080
- There's potatoes and that...
- It's just chicken powder.

774
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:50,880
Wash.

775
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:51,520
Right.

776
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:56,440
Honestly, outsiders

777
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:57,800
say the wildest things.

778
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:01,800
I found it.

779
00:24:03,720 --> 00:24:04,280
Great.

780
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:05,680
Where did you find it?

781
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:06,560
Right here.

782
00:24:06,560 --> 00:24:07,920
Guess my eyesight isn't great.

783
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:08,920
It's okay.

784
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,800
I'll wash these potatoes.

785
00:24:12,350 --> 00:24:13,360
Can I scrub it off?

786
00:24:15,520 --> 00:24:16,360
The "host" is here.

787
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:18,440
Hello.

788
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:19,520
Hello.

789
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:21,120
Have you seen Si?

790
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:22,320
Si went to buy groceries.

791
00:24:23,840 --> 00:24:24,760
Okay.

792
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:27,280
Are you guys cooking?

793
00:24:27,280 --> 00:24:27,680
Yeah.

794
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:28,840
Need any help?

795
00:24:29,240 --> 00:24:29,840
Not really.

796
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:30,720
Just eat.

797
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:34,360
I can't really help with anything.

798
00:24:34,360 --> 00:24:35,400
Me neither.

799
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:36,040
I can't even help

800
00:24:36,040 --> 00:24:36,720
with my own food.

801
00:24:36,720 --> 00:24:37,720
Your own food.

802
00:24:37,720 --> 00:24:38,480
You hold this.

803
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:39,920
Hold this.

804
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:45,440
Here's a shield for you.

805
00:24:45,840 --> 00:24:46,720
Okay, I'll hold it.

806
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:47,680
I'll hold it.

807
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:51,680
You two.

808
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:53,480
I can't anymore.

809
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:57,200
Can you do it with one hand?

810
00:24:57,820 --> 00:24:59,820
(Cracking an egg with one hand)

811
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:03,560
You'll just get egg all over your hand.

812
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:11,480
Can you grab me a pair of chopsticks?

813
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:12,280
Sure.

814
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:21,400
- Here.
- One on each side.

815
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:25,680
What's going on with the pan?

816
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:26,400
You burned it.

817
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:27,720
(Pan sticking)
Isn't the bottom of the pan

818
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:28,280
a little burned.

819
00:25:28,280 --> 00:25:30,040
It's kind of hilarious.

820
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:31,600
Chef, this side is burned.

821
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:32,800
It might taste a little bitter later.

822
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:34,400
How about you...

823
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:34,960
Like this.

824
00:25:35,380 --> 00:25:37,420
(Cleaning the burnt bits off the bottom)

825
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:38,320
This pan isn't very good.

826
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:38,960
He really knows what to say.

827
00:25:42,720 --> 00:25:44,160
He's starting to get ideas.

828
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:44,960
He's got ideas now.

829
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:47,720
It's called dry pot.

830
00:25:47,720 --> 00:25:48,400
Oh, boy.

831
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:49,360
Here we go again.

832
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:50,280
Dry pot chicken.

833
00:25:50,280 --> 00:25:52,480
Dry pot is a little much.

834
00:25:52,480 --> 00:25:53,080
Teasing her.

835
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:54,560
The Kung Pao chicken I get

836
00:25:54,560 --> 00:25:55,880
always has a layer
of oil floating on top.

837
00:25:55,880 --> 00:25:56,760
Yours is pretty healthy.

838
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:58,280
What a compliment.

839
00:25:58,280 --> 00:25:59,080
Okay.

840
00:25:59,600 --> 00:26:01,000
We're having

841
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,600
dry pot chicken tonight.

842
00:26:02,600 --> 00:26:03,800
Dry pot chicken.

843
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:04,640
One's complimenting her,

844
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:05,160
and the other's teasing her.

845
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:06,360
Is the name really that bad?

846
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:11,880
That hurts.

847
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:13,160
Looks really good.

848
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:14,210
It looks so good.

849
00:26:14,220 --> 00:26:15,060
(Looking)

850
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:19,680
Don't laugh, okay?

851
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:25,400
So clingy.

852
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:29,920
Weren't you the one who laughed first?

853
00:26:32,920 --> 00:26:34,080
I was just showing a little respect.

854
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:35,080
Of course.

855
00:26:35,080 --> 00:26:35,600
Just looking at it,

856
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:37,240
I can tell the flavor's

857
00:26:37,240 --> 00:26:37,800
already there.

858
00:26:43,760 --> 00:26:44,520
Smash the garlic.

859
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:49,360
Can I have a bite?

860
00:26:51,760 --> 00:26:52,680
Have some peanuts.

861
00:26:57,020 --> 00:26:58,220
(Glances)

862
00:26:58,600 --> 00:26:59,240
Here, Chef.

863
00:26:59,240 --> 00:27:00,200
Can you help me

864
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:01,120
get a piece of paper, Chen Hewen?

865
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:04,800
Time to show off
his emotional intelligence.

866
00:27:07,520 --> 00:27:08,480
The peanuts are pretty good.

867
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:11,360
Pretty good.

868
00:27:14,560 --> 00:27:15,080
Here, Chef.

869
00:27:15,080 --> 00:27:16,000
How should we plate this?

870
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:16,560
Wait.

871
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:18,880
I need to taste it first.

872
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:20,440
Just to make sure
every piece tastes good.

873
00:27:20,700 --> 00:27:22,080
(Tasting)

874
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:22,720
Let's get a pair of chopsticks.

875
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:23,800
Let's taste it.

876
00:27:25,760 --> 00:27:26,760
I'll grab one too.

877
00:27:27,740 --> 00:27:29,460
(Getting chopsticks)

878
00:27:32,360 --> 00:27:33,040
Is it okay?

